# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the proxy is the only component that holds a payment
# credential. If you ever find yourself putting a key anywhere else -- an
# agent, a test, a notebook -- stop. That would make the project's central
# claim false. See tests/test_no_secrets_in_agent.py.

# ---- signing secret for capability tokens --------------------------------
# Generate one:  python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# Deliberately SEPARATE from the Razorpay key: rotating one must not force
# rotating the other. The proxy refuses to start if this is unset -- there is
# no default, because a default signing secret is the same as no signature.
GATEKEEPER_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ---- Razorpay TEST MODE credentials --------------------------------------
# Dashboard -> Settings -> API Keys -> Generate Test Key
# The backend REFUSES to start with anything that is not an rzp_test_ key.
# This project has no business holding a production credential.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_YOUR_KEY_ID_HERE
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=YOUR_KEY_SECRET_HERE

# ---- optional: LLM for natural-language cart resolution ------------------
# Everything works without this. The agent falls back to keyword matching, and
# the eval never calls an LLM at all (results must be reproducible).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
